# The preferred citation is the dataset and its version on Hugging Face, so that GitHub's "Cite
# this repository" gives the dataset. Zenodo archives each GitHub release of this repository
# (the code and documents, no data) from .zenodo.json, which it reads in place of this file; the
# DOI below stands for all versions of the software and documents and resolves to the latest.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NewsAttention, please cite the dataset and its version as below, and credit Wikipedia's contributors when you use the event text (see the dataset card's How to cite)."
type: software
title: "NewsAttention: software and documentation for a daily dataset of news events and Wikipedia page views"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
abstract: >-
  NewsAttention links each day's news events, as English Wikipedia's Current Events Portal lists
  them, to how many people read the Wikipedia articles each event links to: by language edition
  (exact daily counts from the Wikimedia Analytics API) and by country (Wikimedia's published,
  privacy-protected daily counts, used as published), with measures of attention: baseline,
  lift, excess views, peak day, half-life and breadth. Version 0.1.0 holds 21,997 events from
  2023-02-06 to 2026-11-22 and their daily views from 2023-01-09 to 2026-11-22. This repository
  holds the software that builds and checks the dataset, and its documents.
